  "id": "individuals-with-disabilities-education-act",
  "term": "Individuals With Disabilities Education Act",
  "definition": "The Individuals With Disabilities Education Act (IDEA) is a U.S. special education law that requires schools to identify and evaluate children who may have disabilities and, when eligible, provide a free appropriate public education through an Individualized Education Program. It also includes procedural safeguards intended to support parents’ informed participation in decisions about evaluation, eligibility, and services.",
